\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard

\emph on
Third
\emph default
, we combine the F.O.C.s and solve them as part of one system.
 In this process, we appeal to the tax neutrality result specified by Lemma
 1 to eliminate redundant tax shifters, which are difficult to characterize.
 We then appeal to well-known properties of Marshallian demand functions
 (e.g., 
\emph on
Cournot aggregation
\emph default
 and
\emph on
