Discussion: The Efficacy of Trade and Industrial Policy
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
This section, guided by Theorem 1-3, discusses the efficacy of trade and
 industrial policy in distorted open economies.
 We conjecture that standalone trade policy measures can be ineffective
 even when chosen optimally.
 Unilateral scale correction via industrial policy can also backfire, underscori
ng the importance of international coordination.
 We later test these conjectures by estimating model parameters and utilizing
 our optimal policy formulas.
\emph on

