 Our conjecture is that if industry-level trade and scale elasticities exhibit
 a 
\emph on
strong
\emph default
 negative correlation, the welfare gains from trade policy are limited—a
 claim we evaluate quantitatively in Section 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "sec:Quantifying-the-Gains"
plural "false"
caps "false"
noprefix "false"

\end_inset

.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Conjecture
If industry-level trade and scale elasticities exhibit a strong negative
 correlation (
\begin_inset Formula $\mbox{{Cov\left(\sigma_{k},\mu_{k}\right)\ll0}}$
\end_inset

), standalone trade policy measures deliver limited welfare gains even when
 set optimally.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
A formal evaluation of this conjecture requires estimating model parameters,
 as performed in Sections 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "sec:Estimation"
plural "false"
